  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project for Economic Reintegration Assistance to Potential and Returning Migrant Youth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the initiatives of the Government of Guatemala, including QUEDATE centers and Regional Attention Offices for returning migrants, this project aims to strengthen potential and returning migrant youth capabilities to improve their livelihoods under a human security paradigm. The project will provide market-driven technical and vocational training and will upgrade government facilities to provide effective environments for the provision of humanitarian services to ensure a comprehensive and lasting response. The project is divided into two components; improve market-driven technical education and learning environments for potential and returning migrants; and expand access to humanitarian assistance and services for potential and returning migrant youth.</narrative>
  </description>
